{# Bash tool: Anthropic-style bash_code_execution, or legacy bash. #}
{% set tool_name = namespace.tools.get("bash_code_execution_tool_name")
    or namespace.tools.get("bash_tool_name")
    or "bash_code_execution" %}

{# Unified text editor (command=view|str_replace|create|insert), or legacy leaf tools / wrapper. #}
{% set text_editor_tool = namespace.tools.get("text_editor_code_execution_tool_name")
    or namespace.tools.get("text_editor_tool_name") %}
{% set view_tool = namespace.tools.get("view_tool_name") %}
{% set str_replace_tool = namespace.tools.get("str_replace_tool_name") %}
{% set create_tool = namespace.tools.get("create_tool_name") %}
{% set insert_tool = namespace.tools.get("insert_tool_name") %}
{% set has_unified_text_editor = text_editor_tool is not none %}
{% set has_leaf_text_editor = view_tool or str_replace_tool or create_tool or insert_tool %}
{% set has_text_editor = has_unified_text_editor or has_leaf_text_editor %}

{% set has_present_files = namespace.tools.get("has_present_files") %}
{% set present_files_tool = namespace.tools.get("present_files_tool_name") %}
{% set has_present_server = namespace.tools.get("has_present_server") %}
{% set present_server_tool = namespace.tools.get("present_server_tool_name") %}

{% if layout is not defined or not layout %}{% else %}
{% set workspace = layout | selectattr("name", "equalto", "user") | first %}
{% set outputs = layout | selectattr("name", "equalto", "outputs") | first %}
{% set uploads = layout | selectattr("name", "equalto", "uploads") | first %}
<{{ tool_name }}>
Execute shell commands in an isolated sandbox environment.

**Filesystem layout:**
| Path | Access | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
{% for mount in layout -%}
| `{{ mount.canonical }}` | {{ mount.access }} | {{ mount.description }} |
{% endfor -%}
{% if skills_prefix is defined and skills_prefix -%}
| `{{ skills_prefix }}*/` | ro | Mounted skill content |
{% endif %}
Rules:
- Use absolute paths. `{{ workspace.canonical }}` is the working directory.
- Do not access paths outside the directories listed above.
- Create intermediate work under `{{ workspace.canonical }}`.
- Save every deliverable the user should receive under `{{ outputs.canonical }}`.
{% if has_unified_text_editor -%}
- Prefer `{{ text_editor_tool }}` for reading/editing text files. It takes a `command` of `view`, `str_replace`, `create`, or `insert`, plus `path` and the fields for that command. Use `{{ tool_name }}` for shell work, builds, installs, and non-text files.
{% elif has_leaf_text_editor -%}
- Prefer the file tools for reading/editing text files{% if view_tool or str_replace_tool or create_tool or insert_tool %}: {% if view_tool %}`{{ view_tool }}` (read){% endif %}{% if str_replace_tool %}{% if view_tool %}, {% endif %}`{{ str_replace_tool }}` (edit){% endif %}{% if create_tool %}{% if view_tool or str_replace_tool %}, {% endif %}`{{ create_tool }}` (new file){% endif %}{% if insert_tool %}{% if view_tool or str_replace_tool or create_tool %}, {% endif %}`{{ insert_tool }}` (insert lines){% endif %}{% endif %}. Use `{{ tool_name }}` for shell work, builds, installs, and non-text files.
{% endif -%}
{% if has_present_files %}
**CRITICAL — delivering files to the user (`{{ present_files_tool }}`):**
- Writing a file is NOT enough. Files never appear in the chat UI unless you call `{{ present_files_tool }}`.
- After creating or updating any user-facing deliverable (reports, CSVs, images, PDFs, zips, code, charts, exports, etc.), you MUST call `{{ present_files_tool }}` with the absolute path(s) under `{{ outputs.canonical }}`.
- Call `{{ present_files_tool }}` in the same turn once the files are ready — do not only mention paths in prose.
- Prefer batching: pass every finished deliverable path in one `{{ present_files_tool }}` call.
- If you revise a deliverable, write the new version to `{{ outputs.canonical }}` and call `{{ present_files_tool }}` again.
- Never claim the user can download or open a file unless you already called `{{ present_files_tool }}` successfully for that path.
{% else -%}
- Save any file the user should receive to `{{ outputs.canonical }}`.
{% endif -%}
{% if has_present_server %}
**Exposing running services (`{{ present_server_tool }}`):**
- After starting an HTTP service in the sandbox (web app, Streamlit, Jupyter, etc.), call `{{ present_server_tool }}` with the port so the user gets a clickable URL.
- Starting the process alone does not surface a link; `{{ present_server_tool }}` is required.
{% endif -%}
{% if few_shots == "True" %}
Examples:
- Shell: call `{{ tool_name }}` with command `cat {{ uploads.canonical }}report.csv`
- Write a deliverable: call `{{ tool_name }}` with command `cp analysis.png {{ outputs.canonical }}analysis.png`
{% if has_unified_text_editor -%}
- Read a text file: call `{{ text_editor_tool }}` with `command="view"`, `path="{{ workspace.canonical }}notes.md"`
- Create a text file: call `{{ text_editor_tool }}` with `command="create"`, `path="{{ outputs.canonical }}summary.md"`, `file_text="..."`
- Edit a text file: call `{{ text_editor_tool }}` with `command="str_replace"`, `path="..."`, `old_str="..."`, `new_str="..."`
{% elif has_leaf_text_editor and view_tool -%}
- Read a text file: call `{{ view_tool }}` with path `{{ workspace.canonical }}notes.md`
{% endif -%}
{% if has_present_files -%}
- Then present it: call `{{ present_files_tool }}` with `["{{ outputs.canonical }}analysis.png"]`
- Multiple outputs: write `{{ outputs.canonical }}summary.md` and `{{ outputs.canonical }}data.csv`, then call `{{ present_files_tool }}` once with both absolute paths
{% endif -%}
{% if has_present_server -%}
- Started a server on port 8501: call `{{ present_server_tool }}` with port `8501` (optional `initial_path`)
{% endif -%}
{% endif %}
</{{ tool_name }}>
{% endif %}
